{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules","id":1550863,"title":"Sorcerer - What are you house rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-08T15:56:08-07:00","id":1550863,"title":"Sorcerer - What are you house rules?","content":"Hello, everyone.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned in a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549745-what-is-the-best-sourcebook-and-rules-set-for-sorcerers-hedge-mages\">previous</a> post, when I run a WoD game, I prefer to avoid crossovers and just use the game line as the basis for the chronicle.<br /> <br /> Thus, if I\u2019m running Werewolf, I don\u2019t have dynamic magic, ascended mages, Traditions, or the Technocracy. Instead, linear magic (as described in the Sorcerer books) is the only kind of magic that is available to mortal spellcasters.<br /> <br /> In previous WtA campaigns I\u2019ve run, I\u2019ve used World of Darkness: Sorcerer to create sorcerer NPCs as antagonists and allies, and it worked really well.<br /> <br /> However, recently I acquired the other books (<b>Sorcerer Revised</b> and <b>Sorcerer 20</b>), plus two other great books from SV, <b>Paths of Power</b> and <b>Sorcerer\u2019s Companion</b>.<br /> <br /> After reading all of them, I decided on a heavily house-ruled system for my sorcerers (for using them as both PCs and NPCs), and I\u2019d like to share it with you here.<br /> <br /> As I said above, dynamic magic does not exist.<br /> <br /> The system from Sorcerer Revised is the basis for this, with the following optional rules:<ul><li><b><i>Equal for All</i></b> character creation.</li> </ul><ul><li>The following <b>Backgrounds</b> (from WoD: Sorcerer and Revised) are available for sorcerers: Allies, Arcane, Contacts, Familiar (lesser), Influence, Library, Mana, Mentor, Relic, Resources, Sanctuary, and Status.</li> </ul><ul><li><i><b>Messing with the Variables</b></i> optional rules: Difficulty is effect level + 3; Time is one turn for all spells (rituals still have a casting time of 10 minutes / level, though).</li> </ul><ul><li><i><b>Ignoring aspects</b></i> (from page 60). As per Sorcerer Revised, a Path\u2019s rating determines the maximum level of all the aspects of that path.</li> </ul><ul><li>To cast a spell, the sorcerer needs a number of successes equal to or higher than the effect level he is trying to achieve (maximum possible effect level is the Path\u2019s rating). In the case of rituals, the ritual level determines the minimum number of successes.</li> </ul><br /> So, for example, if the sorcerer has three dots in Conjuration he can cast Conjuration spells using all aspects up to level three and, since this Path has multiple aspects, he can use different ratings for each aspect (highest possible aspect level is the Path's rating, though).<br /> <br /> However, if the sorcerer is using different ratings for a spell's multiple aspects, the highest aspect determines how many successes he must obtain in the activation roll.<br /> <br /> For example: Ayreon, the Wizard, has Conjuration three. He wants to conjure his Glock pistol that is lying on a table 10 meters away on the other side of his alchemical lab. So, this means he is using the following aspects:<br /> <br /> Weight ** (a loaded Glock 17 weighs about 940 g)<br /> Distance *** (the bookcase is farther than 6 meters / 20 feet)<br /> Accuracy ** (this is more than enough to bring the pistol to his hand)<br /> Number * (just a single item)<br /> <br /> Ayreon\u2019s player rolls Dexterity + Occult, Difficulty 6 (his highest aspect rating, <i>distance</i>, is 3 + base 3 = 6), and he needs at least three successes. If he does not get a minimum of three successes, the spell will simply fail.<ul><li><b><i>Counterspell</i></b> and <i><b>Unwaving</b></i>, as per Revised (pg. 63).</li> </ul><ul><li><i><b>Cost</b></i>: each spell or ritual costs one Willpower. Some spells or rituals may have a higher cost.</li> </ul><br /> I\u2019m also using one of the very few rules I liked from Sorcerer 20: non-supernatural witnesses may reduce a sorcerer\u2019s success on his activation roll (see Sorcerer 20th pg. 15).<br /> <br /> And in case someone Is wondering, I use the rules for <i><b>Psychic Powers</b></i> from Sorcerer 20th: roll Willpower to activate. Difficulty is effect level +3. All psychic powers cost one Willpower per use.<br /> <br /> Now, <b>one last question</b> for those more knowledgeable regarding Path of Hellfire:<br /> <br /> Even with a casting time of one round, can a sorcerer cast his spell and attack his target in the same turn? Does the PC have to take a penalty for using multiple dice pools? Or he can only attack in the following turn?<br /> <br /> I remember a house rule some Mage storytellers used back in the day that you could cast your spell and attack with in the same turn without penalty, but I don\u2019t know if that would be too unbalancing.<br /> <br /> Anyway, If you\u2019ve read so far, I thank you.<br /> <br /> And, please, share your sorcerer house-rules if you fell like doing so. I\u2019d love reading them.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T01:40:01-07:00","id":1550874,"title":"","content":"We must have typed out posts at pretty much the same time, I just shared my experience with some house rules in an <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1489265-upgrading-sorcerer?p=1550862#post1550862\">older thread</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greywolf76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules#post1550863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system from Sorcerer Revised is the basis for this, with the following optional rules:<ul><li><b><i>Equal for All</i></b> character creation.</li> </ul><ul><li>The following <b>Backgrounds</b> (from WoD: Sorcerer and Revised) are available for sorcerers: Allies, Arcane, Contacts, Familiar (lesser), Influence, Library, Mana, Mentor, Relic, Resources, Sanctuary, and Status.</li> </ul><ul><li><i><b>Messing with the Variables</b></i> optional rules: Difficulty is effect level + 3; Time is one turn for all spells (rituals still have a casting time of 10 minutes / level, though).</li> </ul><ul><li><i><b>Ignoring aspects</b></i> (from page 60). As per Sorcerer Revised, a Path\u2019s rating determines the maximum level of all the aspects of that path.</li> </ul><ul><li>To cast a spell, the sorcerer needs a number of successes equal to or higher than the effect level he is trying to achieve (maximum possible effect level is the Path\u2019s rating). In the case of rituals, the ritual level determines the minimum number of successes.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much congruent with the house rules I use. Since I have a Medium player, I also kept the Chol\u00e9 Background from Revised. The base casting difficulty actually went up one to +5 for us, because we also use a rule to decrease difficulty with more casting time and a rule to spend successes on Aspects after the roll. Both make casting a lot easier and more effective, so the increase in difficulty isn't that bad to balance things out.<br /> <br /> I allow Willpower regeneration with Meditation because otherwise temporary Willpower is a very limited resource that is hard to replenish, although I'm considering switching to a Mana/Quintessence pool for good since everyone has the Mana Background anyways.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T04:35:30-07:00","id":1550876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules?p=1550874#post1550874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We must have typed out posts at pretty much the same time, I just shared my experience with some house rules in an <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1489265-upgrading-sorcerer?p=1550862#post1550862\">older thread</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was quite a coincidence. Guess we didn't incur any Paradox, here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for sharing your house-rules. You did a great job streamlining the Aspects' table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules?p=1550874#post1550874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty much congruent with the house rules I use. Since I have a Medium player, I also kept the Chol\u00e9 Background from Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot to mention Chol\u00e9 completely. I use that, too. But I tend to restrict it to members of societies with a spiritualist worldview, such as the Uzoma or the Bata'a.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules?p=1550874#post1550874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I allow Willpower regeneration with Meditation because otherwise temporary Willpower is a very limited resource that is hard to replenish,</div> </div> </div> </div>i do that that, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules?p=1550874#post1550874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">although I'm considering switching to a Mana/Quintessence pool for good since everyone has the Mana Background anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking about implementing a 1-10 Mana pool for sorcerers for a while. Each and every splat has its own &quot;magical fuel&quot;, so why not sorcerers?<br /> <br /> I still have to decide upon some points before adopting a Mana Pool, though:<br /> <br /> <b>What would it be the initial Mana? </b><br /> Determined by the Mana Background? Or a fixed amount, just like Willpower?<br /> <br /> <b>How much would it cost to buy permanent Mana points with freebies? And experience points?</b><br /> For reference, <i>Gnosis</i> costs 2 freebies per dot (and current Gnosis x 2 to buy with XP). <i>Glamour</i> costs 3 freebies per dot (and current Glamour x 3 to buy with XP). And Sekhem costs 1 freebie per dot (but it's limited by the PC's Balance rating which cannot be higher than 3 in a starting Mummy PC).<br /> <br /> <b>What would it be used for?</b><br /> Just fueling spells and rituals in place of Willpower? Or does it also lower spellcasting difficulty, just like the Mana Background in Revised? (Personally, I'd like to use Mana for both casting and lowering difficulties).<br /> <br /> <b>How do sorcerers recover Mana?</b><br /> Daily? Through meditation (Perception + Meditation, difficulty 7, each success recovers one point)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","user":"Greywolf76","date":". 05-09-2025, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T06:56:45-07:00","id":1550904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greywolf76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules?p=1550876#post1550876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What would it be the initial Mana? </b><br /> Determined by the Mana Background? Or a fixed amount, just like Willpower?<br /> <br /> <b>How much would it cost to buy permanent Mana points with freebies? And experience points?</b><br /> For reference, <i>Gnosis</i> costs 2 freebies per dot (and current Gnosis x 2 to buy with XP). <i>Glamour</i> costs 3 freebies per dot (and current Glamour x 3 to buy with XP). And Sekhem costs 1 freebie per dot (but it's limited by the PC's Balance rating which cannot be higher than 3 in a starting Mummy PC).</div> </div> </div> </div>Intuitively I would use the same costs &amp; initial value of Willpower, since the new stat would take over much of the function.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greywolf76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules?p=1550876#post1550876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What would it be used for?</b><br /> Just fueling spells and rituals in place of Willpower? Or does it also lower spellcasting difficulty, just like the Mana Background in Revised? (Personally, I'd like to use Mana for both casting and lowering difficulties).</div> </div> </div> </div>Same for me. The option of lowering difficulty as an alternative use adds some variability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greywolf76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules?p=1550876#post1550876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How do sorcerers recover Mana?</b><br /> Daily? Through meditation (Perception + Meditation, difficulty 7, each success recovers one point)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recover one unit automatically when sleeping. As mentioned in the other thread I'm not a big fan of making Abilities quasi-mandatory, so I would allow a Focus roll (Attribute + Ability) as an alternative if the Sorcerer is using their off-time to practice or study.<br /> I also think it would be fair to use external Mana sources (Tass, Mana Manipulation) to temporarily exceed the max Mana pool value. Maybe for a Scene or until sleep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greywolf76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550863-sorcerer-what-are-you-house-rules#post1550863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with a casting time of one round, can a sorcerer cast his spell and attack his target in the same turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Hanging Spells for that, because it rewards players for planning ahead. I just have to remind them sometimes that it's an option they have.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T10:43:13-07:00","id":1550905,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answers and suggestions, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>. Particularly about using Tass (which probably I'll call &quot;Mana crystals&quot; to keep with the sorcerer theme.<br /> <br /> Regarding the meditation and Focus rolls, I'm considering lowering the difficulty to 6 if the sorcerer is in his own Sanctuary or in a place with an abundance of mystical / spiritual energy, such as a Caern.<br /> <br /> And you're right, hanging spells is always a good option (not to mention that adds a Vancian aspect to spellcasting that I really enjoy)<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm editing this post because I have to give credit where credit is due. While reading older threads looking for house-rules for sorcerers, I've found many of the ideas and house-rules proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> to be very helpful. So, thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","user":"Greywolf76","date":". 05-11-2025, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}